[[File:S1E08 Montehue Dante.jpg|thumb|170px|Young Dante with his friendly rival [[Montehue]]]]
When he was young, Dante Vale met [[Metz]], who recognized Dante's potential to be a [[Seeker]]. Through Metz' tutelage, Dante learned about [[magic]] and [[Titans]]. Dante's first [[Amulet]] to bond to, that of [[Solwing]], was found all by himself while spending time in Turkey. {{source|Ladies' Choice}} Dante was also given a [[Caliban]] Amulet by Metz, though Dante took over a year to be able to invoke and master the [[Meso-Titan]] due to Caliban's immense power. Initially, Dante was only able to keep Caliban summoned for about a minute, though Dante increased this time through training. {{source|Huntik.com|Webisodes}} His friendship with Metz also found Dante working alongside [[Eathon Lambert]] and [[Simon Judeau]]. {{source|Huntik.com/Profiles}} As a teenager, he trained intensively under Metz' friend [[Master Storm]] in [[China]] alongside [[Lin Storm]], with whom he formed a close friendship. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Some years later, Dante found another Caliban Amulet in [[South America]], during one of his most dangerous missions for the [[Huntik Foundation]]. {{Source|Caliban Amulet (GP Card)|Caliban Amulet}} Dante kept this a secret, with everyone believing he possessed simply the one Caliban, who had become his most distinctive Titan. {{Source|The Mission}} 

Dante later gained an [[Ignatius]] Amulet while on an expedition to a volcano in [[:Category:Chile|Chile]]. As Ignatius Amulets were common in this country, both Dante and another Seeker acquired one during this expedition. Another Meso-Titan, Dante was able to control much faster after learning how to control Caliban, though Ignatius' flares occasionally would set something, such as buildings, on fire. Three water Titans were once needed to put Ignatius out. {{Source|Huntik.com|Webisodes}}

In his youth, Dante also crossed paths with [[Montehue]], a student of the history of war and fellow treasure hunter, with the pair instantly forming a competitive but nonetheless friendly rivalry. Whilst racing up a mountain, Dante secretly slipped a [[Tolivane]] [[Amulet]] into Montehue's pocket as a way of keeping things fair. After saving Montehue from falling to his death, Dante left a lasting impression on him, and introducing him to the world of [[Seekers]]. The pair's competitive friendship spanned many years, with the pair eventually becoming close friends through working together to use [[Mjolnir]] to defeat [[Ymir]] in the [[Temple of Thor]] and, later, fighting side by side against [[the Professor]] in [[King Solomon's mines]]. {{source|Two Powers Become One}} {{source|To Be Together}}

Dante was manipulated by [[the Professor]] into giving him the [[Rings]] of [[Behemoth]] and [[Tao]] so that he could perform a ritual to summon [[Lord Casterwill]]'s Titan of Immortality, [[Overlos]] which would end the [[Curse of the Legendary Titans]], saving Metz's life. Dante also gave him back his Caliban Amulet, which the Professor had originally used to save Metz' life at the [[Temple of Tecobai]]. Dante saw it as a way of repaying old debts, truly believing that Simon could save Metz one last time. However, it turned out to be a trick, as the Professor had much more evil intentions with the three Legendary Titans. This broke Dante mentally, and caused him to go into a state of shock and grief. {{Source|S1E25}} Lok therefore had to lead the mission to stop the Professor's plan. Dante eventually managed to recover from his stupour and save Zhalia from two [[Undergolem]] Titans. He tried to put right his mistake by helping Lok to stop the Professor and battle the three Legendary Titans. He summoned [[Archwarder]], disrupting the Professor's control over Overlos, allowing Lok to use [[Dendras]] and command Overlos to banish himself and the other three Legendary Titans to the [[Spirit World]]. {{Source|S1E26}}

