[[File:S1E01 Dante Caliban Amulet.png|thumb|170px|Dante with the [[Amulet]] of [[Caliban]]]]
During a mission to rescue [[Clements]] from the [[Ring of Arc]], Dante entered a dreamworld, created by [[Arc]], the Legendary Titan of Fate. Here, Dante had a vision of his own death with Zhalia and his friends crying at his grave. Despite being visibly haunted by this, as to not worry anybody, he kept it to himself and told no one. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}{{source|Lok's Leadership}}{{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}

Dante was left saddened when Zhalia chose to leave the Huntik team, adamant she plays to her strengths and infiltrate the [[Blood Spiral]] to fight them from the inside. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}} Using Zhalia's [[Logosbook]], the pair communicated with one another. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

In the Vault of [[Hernán Cortés]], Dante managed to beat [[Wilder]] in recovering the [[Ring]] of the Legendary Titan of Dimensions, [[Umbra]], the Shadow Jaguar. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

Deeply shaken by the vision of his future and with the threat of the [[Blood Spiral]] looming, Dante returned to train under [[Master Storm]] in [[China]]. After learning the [[Copykind]] spell, he used [[Umbra]] to join his team in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. Using Copykind to mimic [[Ignatius]]' flames, he caused the [[Heart of Vlad Dracul]] to overload and injure [[Tantras]]. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}
[[File:S2E50 Dante 13.png|170px|Dante sacrifices himself to take out the [[Red Comet]]|thumb]]
During the final battle at the [[Spiral Mark]], Dante was able to defeat Rassimov one on one while helping Lok and Sophie destroy [[Legion]]. However, [[the Betrayer]] revealed that he had faked the last prophecies of [[Nostradamus]], and in attempting to destroy the Mark, the team had activated it and sent the [[Red Comet]] hurtling towards Earth. Realizing the time had come to fulfill his destiny that Arc had revealed, Dante died sacrificing himself to prevent the [[Red Comet]] from hitting the Earth. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}

Attempting to destroy his enemies' will to fight, the Betrayer revealed Dante's death to the [[Huntik Foundation]] and  the [[Casterwill family]], devastating [[Zhalia Moon]], [[Metz]], and [[Montehue]]. However, Lok, enraged at the Spirals' mocking of Dante's sacrifice, made a motivating speech, inspiring the Foundation to finish what Dante started, knowing he would have believed they could win the war without him. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

During the Betrayer's ritual, Dante's ashes were teleported back to Earth by [[Umbra]]. By using the [[Copykind]] spell on [[Phoenix]], the Legendary Titan of the Rebirth, just prior to his death, Dante was able to rise back to life from his ashes. Dante soon attempted to prevent the Betrayer from invoking the [[Nullifiers]], battling him; however, his [[Hyperstride]]<nowiki/>s couldn't keep up with the Betrayer's ability to fly, and he was knocked down and almost made immobile by the Betrayer's [[Shadowlock]] spell. Lok and Sophie, though, were quick to find a prophecy in Nostradamus' real writings, telling Dante to hold the Betrayer, which he did so with [[Stoneglove]] paired with [[Doublespell]], allowing Lok to throw the [[Willblade]] at the Betrayer, revealing this weakness -- the Spiral mark on his back, thus enabling the team to finally stop the Betrayer. After the defeat of [[the Betrayer]], Dante Vale became a member of the [[Huntik Foundation Council]], leaving leadership of his old team to [[Lok Lambert]]. {{Source|Dante's Return}}

[[File:S2E35 Dante Zhalia hug.png|190px|thumb|Dante and Zhalia say goodbye]]
Dante initially knew of Zhalia as a fellow Foundation Seeker, and had a lot of respect for her skills, asking her to help the Huntik team in Prague after their first meeting. {{Source|S1E03}} While other members of his team, particularly [[Sophie Casterwill]], took a distrust to her, Dante saw her as reliable and trustworthy, letting her prove herself to the team by rescuing [[Peter]] in Rouen. {{Source|S1E04}} Dante assured Zhalia that he trusted her after asking her to deliver [[DeFoe]]'s Amulets which meant a great deal to her as nobody had ever told her that. {{Source|S1E10}}  Over time, the pair began to develop feelings for one another {{Source|S1E17}}, and despite Zhalia's betrayal of his team to [[Klaus]], Dante understood her reasons and forgave her. {{Source|S1E17}} After the explosion at her [[Zhalia's apartment|apartment]], the pair almost kissed but were interrupted by [[Lok Lambert]]. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} They grew deeply protective of one another {{Source|S1E23}} {{source|S2E27}} and Zhalia later admitted that Dante meant more to her than anything else in the world. {{source|S1E25}} 

When Zhalia chose to leave the team to infiltrate the [[Blood Spiral]], Dante was deeply saddened but understood why she had to go. {{Source|S2E35}} They stayed in touch by writing in a pair of [[Logosbook]] journals {{source|S2E36}} from which even [[Tantras]] could tell Zhalia cared for him a great deal. {{Source|S2E39}} When Zhalia discovered Dante had sacrificed himself to stop the [[Red Comet]], she was devastated. {{Source|S2E51}} However, Dante wrote her a final message revealing his ultimate secret plan, and Zhalia was overjoyed when he rose from the ashes. {{Source|S2E52}}

[[File:S2E37 Dante Caliban eyes.png|thumb|200px|Dante and [[Caliban|Powerbonded Caliban]] have perfect telepathic communication]]
Dante is both a leader and tactician for his team, employing his intellect, experience, and knowledge of history to push his team forward. Having trained in both martial arts and the abilities of a [[Seeker]], his combat style combines the two into a formidable force with either enhancing the other. Depending on the situation, he can use spells to augment his agility, enhance his martial arts, attack at a range, or provide shielding. All of this is combined with his impressive stamina and endurance, being able to withstand two days of non-stop walking without any food, water or sleep before finally passing out and still being able to invoke Titans and use spells shortly after. However, Dante was shown to be completely exhausted when he invoked Caliban, Metagolem and Behemoth within a short span of time. {{Source|S1E21}} 

Over the years, Dante has amassed a vast and varied collection of [[Titans]] through his many adventures. He stores most of his Amulets in concealed safes and drawers inside his home. {{Source|The Casterwill Client}} {{Source|S1E07}} Although he relies primarily on a core group of Titans, he chooses to bring other Titans from his collection when specific missions call for different abilities. {{Source|S1E07}} {{Source|S1E23}} He has a close bond with several of his Titans due to the time spent training together, most notably his signature Titan, [[Caliban]] to whom he is now [[Powerbonded]]. {{Source|S2E35}}

