===[[Grier]]===
[[File:S1E12 Grier Dante explosion.jpg|190px|thumb|Dante and Grier face off]]
Dante had an intense rivalry with [[Grier]], as both were powerful and charismatic Seekers harboring strong values. The more the two fought, the more they recognized that the other was fighting for the good of mankind, though both had very different ideas of this good. Extremely well-matched in physical combat, their conflicts were often resolved between their two gargantuan [[Titans]]: Dante's [[Metagolem]] and Grier's signature Titan, the bear-brawler, [[Breaker]], with this fighting rivalry reaching its peak when the two men battled it out on [[Sutos Island]]. Grier himself stated that he had waited his whole life to fight an opponent like Dante {{Source|Like Father, Unlike Son}} and Lok described their relationship to [[Den Fears]] as having been that of archenemies. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

=== [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] ===
While initially Dante only accepted [[Sophie Casterwill|Sophie]] and [[Lok Lambert|Lok]]'s offer to help the latter find [[Eathon Lambert|his father]] as a paid job, he quickly bonded with them and was willing to take a [[Raypulse]] spell for [[Sophie Casterwill|Sophie]] the same day he took took the job. {{Source|The Casterwill Client}} Dante went as far as to reverse the roles and briefly return to his work as a private investigator to afford a trip relating to the search for [[Eathon Lambert]] and the [[Amulet of Will]] when Sophie's bank accounts were wiped. {{Source|All Work and No Pay}} Much like [[Metz]] was a mentor to Dante, he also taught Sophie and Lok many aspects of the [[Seekers|Seeker]] life; this is more noteworthy with Lok, who after charged with leading a mission complemented Dante's leadership. {{Source|Lok's Leadership}}<blockquote>''Sophie, take care of Lok. Make sures he grows up just like his father.'' <br/> - Dante to Sophie before seemingly sacrificing himself to destroy the [[Red Comet]]
</blockquote>

